        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0f936c3e-2da3-53fe-a696-ffc2ac8aacd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kool Kojak, Danny DeVito, Ed Helms, Zac Efron, Victoria Justice, Savan Kotecha, Mehrdad Raissi Ardali\n- Works: The Lorax, Best Friend's Brother, Victorious, The Lorax soundtrack, animated films\n- Roles: cast members, songwriter, producer, Persian voice actor\n- Topics: artist collaborations, film casting, soundtrack credits, dubbed animation voices\n\nFacts:\n- Kool Kojak has written and produced for artists including Sean Paul, Yelle, Waka Flocka Flame, Travis Barker, Britney Spears, Jesse and Joy, Andy Milonakis, Icona Pop, N.A.S.A., Dirt Nasty, Lordz of Brooklyn, Ursula 1000, Warren G, and Dr. Seuss's The Lorax.\n- The film The Lorax includes Danny DeVito as the Lorax, Ed Helms as the Once-ler, and Zac Efron as Ted in its cast.\n- The song Best Friend's Brother was produced by Kool Kojak.\n- Kool Kojak co-wrote Best Friend's Brother with Savan Kotecha and Victoria Justice.\n- Best Friend's Brother was created for the 2011 soundtrack to the Nickelodeon television series Victorious.\n- Mehrdad Raissi Ardali provided the Persian voice for the Once-ler in The Lorax.\n- Mehrdad Raissi Ardali has also provided Persian voices for animated characters including Donkey in Shrek, Marty in Madagascar, Buck, Bolt in Bolt, Carl Fredricksen in Up, Flynn Rider in Tangled, RJ in Over the Hedge, Francesco Bernoulli in Cars 2, Mr. Ping in Kung fu Panda, Ramon in Happy Feet 2, the Man in the Yellow Hat in Curious George, Raoul in A Monster in Paris, Kevin, Barry in Bee Movie, Bunnymund in Rise of the Guardians, Guy in The Croods, and Kristoff in Frozen.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
